{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310742,"nonce":"phPf/0jKXqLkAxUniSsnhXpkxMM=","title":"An untyped lambda parameter falls back to Dynamic when the callee's formal involves a class type parameter, so the body dereferences a raw ...","message":"**FIXED 1fb6a169**: Issue2378 now passes UNANNOTATED. The Array-receiver hint types the lambda parameter to the element, and the indirect call boxes a String into a `Dynamic` formal. See [[bugs-stdlib-silent-wrong-answers-eight-defects]] D1.\n\n`var vs:Array\u003cString\u003e = [\"abcd\"]; vs.map(function(v) return v.length)` SIGSEGVs.\nAnnotating the parameter (`function(v:String)`) fixes it. Corpus proof: Issue2378\ngoes CRASH -\u003e PASS with only `:String` added to its two lambda params.\n\nThe lambda's untyped params default to Dynamic, MIR formals become `*void`, and\nthe caller hands over a raw element the body dereferences. The compiler's own doc\ncomment at `compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering/mod.rs:799-807` already describes this\nexact failure.\n\nATTRIBUTION IS CONFOUNDED — do not fix from the first story alone. The original\nclaim blamed `resolve.rs:456`, whose `TypeKind::Class {..} =\u003e Some(id), _ =\u003e None`\ndrops the hint for Array/Map/String/Interface receivers. A verifier isolated a\nSECOND, independently sufficient trigger: **a class type parameter in the formal**\ncrashes even with a Class receiver (`class Gen\u003cT\u003e` with `apply(f:T-\u003eInt)` -\u003e 139),\nwhile a method-generic formal on a non-generic class is fine. So widening the\nreceiver match alone will NOT fix `Array.map`; the type argument must also be\nsubstituted into the formal.\n\nRELATED, separate defect: a local binding of function type whose name+arity\ncollides with a stdlib static gets bound to the NATIVE symbol. `function\nappend(v:Int)` is rewritten to `file_append_default` (`call/mod.rs:1263`\n`.or_else(find_unique_static_by_name_and_params)`, `runtime_mapping.rs:2128`).\nRenaming the local fixes it. Scope is WIDER than \"local named functions\": a plain\n`var append = function(v:Int) {...}` hits it too, so a fix must exclude ANY local\nbinding of function type.\n\nClosures are NOT a driver of crashes: closure-bearing files are 17.5% of CRASH vs\n14.5% of the corpus and 13.5% of PASS (~1.4 sigma, no enrichment), and 38 of the\n40 closure CRASH tests reproduce identically on macOS. See\n[[bugs_mac_and_linux_conformance_are_identical]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_untyped_lambda_param_becomes_dynamic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}